risk                 package:AA                      R Documentation

Survival of Multiple Myeloma Patients

Description:

     The 'risk' data frame has 21 rows and 4 columns.

     Data on survival of multiple myeloma patients following two
     different chemotherapy treatments in a Cancer and Leukaemia Group
     B trial.  The data contain outcomes for 156 patients at 21
     institutions, an average of 7.4 patients per institution.

Usage:

     data(risk)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'n1' the number of patients following treatment method one;

     'y1' the number of survival patients following treatment method
          one;

     'n2' the number of patients following treatment method two;

     'y2' the number of survival patients following treatment method
          two.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Lipsitz, S.R., Dear, K.B.G., Laird, N.M. and Molenberghs, M.
     (1998).  Tests for homogeneity of the risk difference when data
     are sparse.  _Biometrics_, *54*, 148-160.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 4.4.

Examples:

     data(risk)
     attach(risk)
     boxplot(y1/n1, y2/n2, xlab = "treatment method", ylab = "proportion of survival")
     detach()
